<title>USA: Merrill says to price $2.8 bln N.J. deal June 25.</title>
<headline>Merrill says to price $2.8 bln N.J. deal June 25.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co plans to price New Jersey's $2.75 billion taxable pension funding bonds on June 25, with a retail order period beginning on Monday, the firm said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The taxable bonds will be used to pay off the unfunded liability in the state's pension system, and in the process free up about $590 million of one-shot budget savings for Gov Christine Whitman.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
